LICENSE — NOT YET FINALIZED

This repository's tooling, scripts, and recompiled-runtime code (everything
here EXCEPT any file derived from the game itself — which this repo does not
and must not contain, see .gitignore and README.md) needs a license chosen by
the repository owner before the project is made public. This file is a
placeholder so contributors see the topic has not been skipped, not a
license grant.

Suggested options for the owner to pick from (not a decision made on the
owner's behalf):

1. MIT or Apache-2.0 — simple, permissive, standard for small reverse-
   engineering tooling projects. Apache-2.0 additionally includes an express
   patent grant, which matters more if the runtime code could be seen as
   implementing patented hardware behavior (relevant here, since this is a
   console CPU/GPU reimplementation).
2. GPL-3.0 (or LGPL-3.0 for the runtime library specifically) — copyleft,
   common in emulation/recomp projects (e.g. many N64/PS2 recomp forks use
   GPL family licenses) specifically to prevent closed-source redistribution
   of derived recompiled runtimes.
3. A dual approach some recomp projects use: permissive license (MIT/Apache)
   for the pipeline/tooling scripts, GPL-family for the runtime library that
   the recompiled game code links against — mirrors how the upstream
   PS2Recomp fork this project depends on is licensed. Worth checking what
   license PS2Recomp itself uses (https://github.com/cloudalister/PS2Recomp)
   before choosing, for compatibility.

Regardless of which is chosen, this LICENSE only ever covers the tooling and
runtime code written for this project. It cannot and does not grant any
right to Rockstar Games' or Take-Two's copyrighted game content — this
project produces no such content and none is included here.
